# Rewritten Text

A computer-executed technique for regulating entry to a protected resource belonging to a resource provider within a networked computing environment, where a blockchain—accessible across the network and containing cryptographically signed entries confirmed by distributed miner software—is utilized. This technique encompasses:

Establishing a role-based access definition that specifies the permission set governing resource entry;

Creating a specialized cryptocurrency designed to signal authorized resource access, comprising exchangeable value units linked to blockchain entries, with all cryptocurrency exchanges between these entries subject to miner verification;

Accepting an incoming request from a verified consumer seeking permission to utilize the resource; and

Initiating a blockchain transaction directed to the miner components, transferring a specified cryptocurrency amount into the consumer's blockchain entry—this transaction carries a role identifier, thereby marking the consumer's record as possessing authorized access consistent with the established role parameters.

